The attached image illustrates the physical characterization of Nano-11 alpha-D-glucan nanoparticles. The left panel, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, shows spherical nanoparticles with irregular, cauliflower-like surfaces, appearing mostly as single particles or occasional pairs. The scale bar indicates 50 nm. The right panel displays a particle size distribution histogram, revealing that the nanoparticles have a fairly uniform diameter ranging from 30 to 110 nm, with a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter between 75 and 80 nm. This characterization is crucial as particle size affects cellular uptake and the magnitude of the immune response, supporting Nano-11's utility as a vaccine adjuvant.